# Project defaults

- Change only what the task needs. Do not refactor broadly unless asked.
- Do not commit, push, amend, force-push, or change git config unless the user explicitly asks.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens, private keys).
- Read real files in the repo before concluding how something works. Do not invent APIs, paths, or owners.
- If a decision is blocked by missing info, ask one short question instead of guessing.
- Prefer the smallest clear fix over a large redesign.
